' Activity Diagram 03 — the Δ positive-feedback ratchet: buggy vs fixed.
'
' Two side-by-side lanes (split) contrasting the finality-lag dynamics:
'   - BUGGY: an uncached Θ(Δ²·V) floor walk whose propose cost feeds back into
'     finalization lag (slope > 1 at every equilibrium) → Δ runs away → crosses
'     the 256 cap → SILENT single-parent fallback drops co-parent writes (S5).
'   - FIXED: a persisted frontier pivot + amortized-O(1) up-walk → zero feedback
'     → Δ bounded → over-cap yields a deterministic Err (park / reject), never a
'     lossy substitution.
'
' NOTE on node coloring in THIS PlantUML build: the correct form is the suffix
' stereotype  ':label; <<#hex>>'  (the prefix '#hex:label;' form is deprecated
' here and emits an in-image warning banner). Verified by rendering.
'
' Wolfram reference: formal/wolfram/finalized_floor/delta_ratchet.wl proves the
' buggy feedback slope > 1 (unstable) and the fixed advance has zero feedback.
'
' Source of truth for the ratchet figure in
' docs/theory/finalized-floor/finalized-floor-verification.md (section 2).
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/theory/finalized-floor/diagrams/03-delta-ratchet.puml

@startuml 03-delta-ratchet
!theme plain

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor        #FFFFFF
  BorderColor            #333333
  ArrowColor             #444444
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  DiamondBorderColor     #E65100
}
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title The Δ-ratchet ── buggy Θ(Δ²·V) floor walk (runaway) vs fixed O(1) up-walk (bounded)

' Node color legend (suffix <<#hex>> form):
'   red    (#FFEBEE / #FFCDD2 / #EF9A9A) = buggy step / cliff / write-loss
'   green  (#E8F5E9 / #C8E6C9)           = fixed step / safe outcome
'   amber diamonds (#FFF8E1)             = Δ-cap decision

start
split
  -[#C62828]-> BEFORE the fix;
  partition "BUGGY ── Θ(Δ²·V) uncached floor walk" #FFEBEE {
    repeat
      :propose cost ∝ Δ²\n(uncached ft_witnessed at every step,\nΘ(Δ·V) per parent, Θ(Δ²·V) total); <<#FFEBEE>>
      :finalization lags\n(finalize throughput falls as\npropose cost ∝ Δ² rises); <<#FFEBEE>>
      :Δ = num(maxParent) − num(floor)\nGROWS; <<#FFEBEE>>
    repeat while (Δ still below cap 256 ?) is (positive feedback\nslope > 1 ⟹ Δ runs away) not (Δ ≥ 256)
    :Δ crosses the cap 256\n(the cliff fires); <<#FFCDD2>>
    :SILENT single-parent fallback ──\nreturn highest parent's post_state,\nco-parent writes DROPPED\n(safety S5 / ¬T-K1 / ¬T-NDA); <<#EF9A9A>>
    kill
  }
split again
  -[#2E7D32]-> AFTER the fix;
  partition "FIXED ── persisted pivot + O(1) up-walk" #E8F5E9 {
    :persisted frontier pivot F(X)\n+ incremental up-walk ──\namortized O(1) oracle calls\n(advances telescope to spine length); <<#E8F5E9>>
    :Δ bounded\n(flat — ZERO feedback,\nno runaway back-edge); <<#E8F5E9>>
    if (Δ > cap 256 ?) then (yes)
      :over-cap ⟹ deterministic Err\n(propose PARKS the round;\nvalidate REJECTS — both sides\ncompute the same Δ ⟹ no fork)\nNEVER a lossy substitution; <<#C8E6C9>>
      kill
    else (no)
      :merge proceeds on\nfloor.post_state base\n(all band writes folded in); <<#C8E6C9>>
      kill
    endif
  }
end split

legend bottom
  Wolfram  formal/wolfram/finalized_floor/delta_ratchet.wl — over the reals,
  parameter-free: the buggy Θ(Δ²) advance is structurally UNSTABLE (feedback
  slope > 1 at every equilibrium) while the fixed O(1) advance has ZERO
  feedback (Δ stable). The ratchet collapses; over-cap becomes safe.
endlegend

@enduml
